form>` for each maybe. Or CSS keyframes with `transform: translateX(0)` to(-60px), opacity 0.6→0. Use classes with delays. No transform-origin needed. Browser supports.\n- Little dust puffs near rear wheel contact (250,565): circles with CSS scaling/fading. Maybe `animation: puff 1.2s ease-out infinite;` transform-origin. Could use opacity float via SMIL. Just 2 small circles with animate `r`, `opacity`? SMIL animate attributes cx/cy. Use `<animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0.5;0\" dur=\"1.1s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>` and animateTransform translate. Nice. But could clutter. Keep subtle.\n\n- Road dashes: use `<path d=\"M 40 610 H 960\" stroke=\"#c89d5b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"34 44\">` with animated dashoffset. Also lane path at y 650 maybe. Add static markings not under wheels? The road markings move left. CSS animation on stroke-dashoffset.\n- Path edge stones etc static.\n\nBackground:\nLet's sketch:\nSky rect.\nSun circle.\nClouds: shapes using ellipses around x 120,y120 and x 620,y80 maybe; opacity .6. Animate clouds translateX(-20) over 12s alternate ease-in-out. But background motion should imply forward. Slow.\nDistant sea: path from (0,385) Q ... (1000,400) L1000 470 L0 470. Fill #7cc8cf. Add horizontal wave strokes #ffffff opacity .25 at y 400,420,440. Maybe a sailboat? The pelican might be on seaside boardwalk. Add tiny sailboat at (120,408): hull and triangular sail, static. Cute but maybe too detailed. Add 2 distant sailboats at left.\nShore: A wave line where sea meets sand at y=455. Draw cream/gold shape from 0,455 to 1000,450 etc.\nPromenade: fill #e9cf9b from y=470 to 700 with a path top curve. Path surface from 0,515 to 1000,505 etc fill #e8c984. Add edge line.\nSome low bushes/grass at edges. But too much can distract. Maybe stylized coastal grasses at left bottom (x 40, y 570) and right (x 960,y 570), dark teal; gives framing. Also a few pebbles.\n\nMaybe bike and pelican are more important.