{"type":"thinking","text":"Poses look plausible though knee sweep wide x up to 523. At top near path knee at 521,334 and foot 484,422. Fine.\n\nStatic d values use first. Need ensure when animate d, if SMIL not supported, first static.\n\nNow let's think about rendering. We can write file iteratively. Maybe create initial version with all elements. Let's use write tool.\n\nBefore writing, think through path coordinates and aesthetic. Let's construct SVG with comments for structure. Use IDs for gradients/filters. Need possibly output size <100KB.\n\nLet's write initial version.\n\nDetailed code plan:\n\n```\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 700\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"title desc\">\n<title id=title>A pelican riding a bicycle</title>\n<desc id=desc>...</desc>\n<defs>\n <linearGradient id=sky ...>\n ...\n <filter id=softBlur x=...>\n ...\n <style><![CDATA[\n   @keyframes bob ...\n   ...\n ]]></style>\n</defs>\n<rect ...>\n<g id=background> ...</g>\n<g id=speed-lines> ...\n<g id=ground> ...\n<g id=shadow>...\n<!-- far leg -->\n<g id=far-leg ...\n<path ... d=...> <animate .../> ...\n<!-- wheels -->\n...\n<!-- chain -->\n...\n<!-- far crank/pedal/foot -->\n<g id=crank-rotor transform=rotate(25 465 470)>\n <animateTransform.../>\n <g id=far-crank>...\n ...\n</g>\n...\n```\n\nBut layering issue for near leg and crank. Need structure carefully.\n\nLet's map layer order:\n\n1. defs & background\n2. backdrop details (clouds, sea, path)\n3. distant weather / speed lines maybe behind rider\n4. ground shadow\n5. far leg (behind everything)\n6. wheels (rear/front) (front wheel maybe later? front wheel in front of frame and pelican? Should front wheel be behind fork but all wheel body behind frame? Wheel is near side? Both wheels span. Draw wheels then frame over, okay.)\n7. chain\n8. far crank foot? If chainring later, far foot may be obscured. We want far crank and foot behind chainring, but front of frame? Let's