{"type":"thinking","text":"Could use 16 spokes. Add a second set slightly offset with opacity .25 to look like 32? not necessary.\n\nFrame:\nDraw backdrop tube shadow maybe:\n```\n<g fill=none stroke-linecap=round>\n<path d=... stroke=\"#084c45\" stroke-width=18/>\n<path ... stroke=\"url(#frameGrad)\" stroke-width=12/>\n<path ... stroke=\"#2bb3a6\" stroke-width=3 opacity=.7/> maybe highlights on top edges but along entire path wrong.\n```\nBetter use only one stroke with gradient and a subtle darker stroke outline under. The gradient along objectBoundingBox per path might vary each path; define `gradientUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\"` x1=250 y1=300 x2=760 y2=500. Nice. All paths get same gradient.\nFrame highlight: draw a narrow white line offset? Could just use stroke #1b958b for all tubes and add small light dash near top. A 2-tone tube via base dark width 16, overlay gradient width 11. Good.\n\nChainstay etc. Use a single group to apply consistent.\n```\n<g fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n <path d=\"...\" stroke=\"#073c39\" stroke-width=\"18\"/>\n <path d=\"...\" stroke=\"url(#frameGrad)\" stroke-width=\"12\"/>\n</g>\n```\nAll frame tubes. Then head tube maybe width 24/18. Fork separate silver? Frame color teal. Fork dark charcoal or teal. Maybe front fork in teal.\n- Seatpost silver: line from (395,352) to (376,339) width 9 with dark outline.\n- Handlebar dark charcoal with silver highlights.\n- Add cable housing a curved line from handlebar to down tube, in #445. Nice detail.\n\nChain:\n```\n<path d=\"M465 434 L290 454 A16 16 0 0 0 290 486 L465 506 A36 36 0 0 0 465 434 Z\" fill=none stroke=\"#4d5a61\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\">\n <animate attributeName=\"stroke-dashoffset\" .../>\n</path>\n```\nDashes animate at 0.4s; maybe chainring covers ends. Need upper/lower tangent line not necessarily exact. Fine.\n- rear cog circle r=18 fill #445 with teeth dash.\n- Chainring drawn later as circle r=32.\n\nChainring:\n```\n<g>\n <circle cx=465 cy=470 r=34 fill=\"#c7d3d6\" stroke=\"#647880\" stroke-width=3 stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n <circle r=28 fill=\"#2e3d43\"/>\n <g stroke=\"#9fb1b7\" width=3> 5 spokes...\n</g>\n```\nBut rotating chainring with crank. We can include chainring in rotor group, with static transform? The chainring should rotate with group; its teeth dashes. We want far crank behind it, near arm in front. Put far arm before chainring, near arm after in rotor group. This group is drawn after frame? Wait frame should overlay far crank but chainring near side in front of frame. If whole rotor after frame, far arm also in front of frame. Far arm at far side should be behind frame, but visually crank arm over chainstay could be fine? Better split: far arm outside rotor after chain? The far crank rotation would need same animate. Could duplicate animation. Fine. Structure:\n- far crank arm group (with its own animateTransform) + far pedal/foot group (with both parent and child animations). But far foot needs counter rotation. We can nest inside far crank group with animate transform. This group drawn before frame.\n- chainring+near crank group drawn after frame with animateTransform rotate 25→385. Inside include chainring, near arm, near pedal/foot.\n\nYes duplicate animation values. Crank arms both synchronized. Fine. Far crank foot group needs counter-rotate. Great.\n- Far crank group drawn after chain and far leg? We currently have far leg. Draw far crank and foot after wheels/chain before frame. Then frame overlays. Far foot still visible through gap? Frame only thin tubes, so fine. Chainring before? If far crank drawn before frame, chainring after frame. okay.\n- Chainring group after frame and before pelican. Includes near crank arm? But near leg drawn after body later, then near crank should be drawn after near leg. If near crank group drawn after near leg, it includes chainring? Chainring then would overlay near leg, which could hide leg where it crosses. The near leg from hip to pedal crosses over chainring at around x480,y430. In reality near leg in front of chainring. So chainring should be before near leg. Thus:\n   - frame\n   - chainring static? It rotates with near crank but can be separate group. Need two groups with same animation (chainring rotor and near crank rotor). Duplicated animation but synchronized. Fine.\n   - chainring group animate\n   - saddle\n   - pelican body\n   - near leg\n   - near crank/foot group animate\n   This yields chainring behind near leg, near crank/foot in front. Good.\n- The chainring and near crank are both on same axis and same animation, so they stay sync. Great.\n\n- Could put chainring plus a small spider, drawn before pelican. Yes.\n\nFar foot layering behind frame: frame covers chainstay but not much else. Fine.\n\nSaddle:\n- Seatpost from frame seat cluster S=(395,352) to (376,340), metallic.\n- Saddle leather shape at (365,333):\n```\n<path d=\"M 322 333 C 330 323 355 320 383 324 C 399 326 408 331 407 337 C 405 344 389 345 370 344 C 350 343 330 341 322 337 Z\" fill=\"#8a5537\" stroke=\"#5d3622\"/>\n```\nBody bottom 340 will cover top middle maybe. Add springs at x340? Maybe.\n- Maybe draw saddle after body? The bird sits on it: saddle top should be hidden behind bird, but front nose may peek out at (405,330). If body overlaps, visible edges. Drawing before body is correct.\n- Add seatpost near.\n\nPelican:\n- Tail behind body but after saddle.\n- Body path.\n- Neck (should be drawn before body or after? Neck behind chest. Draw neck first then body so body covers base. Head above.)\n- Legs are later.\n- Wing after body, overlapping.\n- Head after neck.\n- Scarf after neck before wing? Around neck base.\n- Beak, helmet, eye.\n\nLet's define body path more elegantly:\n```\n<path d=\"M 336 291\n C 331 261 346 229 379 210\n C 411 191 462 190 496 207\n C 527 222 538 252 531 280\n C 522 316 489 338 448 344\n C 405 350 361 337 342 315\n C 337 308 335 299 336 291 Z\"\n```\nBody center 434,267, bottom 344, front chest 531. Tail at 336. Saddle is x322-407 y333; body bottom left covers part. Saddle nose at 407 visible perhaps. Hip H=445,350 just below body, good.\nMaybe chest should angle down to neck. Neck starts at x505,236. \n- Add darker belly underside path `M 357 315 C 390 336 442 342 483 330` stroke etc.\n- Add feather tufts on lower body: little scallops along bottom maybe. Could add 3 light-gray arcs.\n- Add wing after body.\n\nNeck path:\n```\nM 492 246\nC 505 220 539 228 550 209\nC 560 192 565 174 582 164\nC 601 153 626 160 637 177\nC 645 188 646 200 640 210\nC 626 232 606 247 590 260\nC 566 279 523 276 505 263\nC 495 256 488 252 492 246 Z\n```\nBut head at (619,180), and this neck might look too thick/overlap. Let's okay.\nMaybe neck S:\nM 496 250\nC 504 222 530 222 540 206\nC 551 188 557 170 574 160\nC 590 151 611 153 626 165\nC 641 177 644 194 635 207\nC 622 228 605 241 588 255\nC 566 273 533 278 510 267\nC 500 262 493 257 496 250 Z\nHead overlaps.\n\nCould add neck shading path along back:\nM 507 248 C 517 225 538 224 547 205 C 557 185 563 169 580 161 stroke #ddd6c7.\n\nHead ellipse cx=621 cy=178 rx=44 ry=41. If neck ends at 626,165 etc. Head covers.\nHead shape maybe more pelican: crown slightly flattened:\n`M 580 177 C 577 151 594 133 619 132 C 644 131 661 149 661 174 C 661 197 644 212 622 213 C 599 213 582 199 580 177 Z` This is roundish. Helmet atop.\n- The beak base begins at x=650,y170; good.\n- Eye at (635,168) white ring? draw.\n\nBeak:\nBase around (643,170). Pouch.\n\nHelmet: path over head top:\n```\nM 583 166\nC 580 140 597 120 622 119\nC 646 118 661 134 661 157\nC 661 164 657 169 650 167\nC 633 155 604 154 589 165\nZ\n```\nAdd brim small ellipse `M 654 158 C 666 158 671 163 669 167 C 664 170 657 166 654 163 Z` color darker.\n- Vent slits: `M 603 134 C 612 129 624 127 634 130` stroke.\n- Helmet stripe white/cream.\n- Maybe a tiny headlamp on helmet front at (657,150) yellow circle. Cute but not necessary.\n- Helmet should look like pelican is active. Let's include.\n\nEye at (636,168): black circle r=6.2; golden ring r=8 fill none stroke #d69a36 width 2; highlight. Brow line from (625,158) to (643,160) maybe angled determined. A white eye ring? Pelican eye often yellow. Draw outer pale yellow ellipse rx=9 ry=8, black pupil. Add white highlight.\n\nPouch:\nUpper beak bright golden:\n```\nM 643 166\nC 685 158 740 164 787 181\nC 810 189 823 198 82","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_SNemAlmmgtG5iYdrtJFe1815","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport math\n# generate spoke snippets for convenience\nfor cx,cy,r in [(290,470,94),(735,470,94)]:\n    for i in range(16):\n        a=math.radians(i*22.5)\n        print(f'<line x1=\"{cx}\" y1=\"{cy}\" x2=\"{cx+r*math.cos(a):.1f}\" y2=\"{cy+r*math.sin(a):.1f}\"/>')\nPY","description":"Regenerate spoke markup for embedding"}}
