are 4 repeated animations: first far underlay, second far overlay, third near underlay, fourth near overlay. Extract all. Good.\nThen replace each path d base with values[frame]. Since under/overlay pairs share same list.\n- There are multiple d attrs with same base. We can iterate all paths containing `animate` with attributeName d and replace. But after removing animations, we need map.\nCould use regex per path block:\n```\npath_pattern = re.compile(r'<path d=\"(M 430\\.0 345\\.0[^\"]*)\"([^>]*)>(.*?)</path>', re.S)\n```\nFor each path, get its animation values inside, choose index. Replace.\nSimilarly near.\n- For transforms: after remove all animateTransform, set static transform strings:\n  - `transform=\"rotate(25 465 470)\"` occurrences: far crank group, chainring group, near crank group = 3. Replace all with 133 etc.\n  - foot child `transform=\"rotate(-25 511 470)\"` -> -133.\n  - far foot `transform=\"rotate(-25 419 470)\"` -> -133.\n  - wheel groups currently no transform on inner g. We can add transform=\"rotate(60 290 470)\" to group? find `<g>\\n      <animateTransform ... rearwheel` but after removal, g is empty. Could leave wheels static.\n- Body bob not applied. Fine.\nThen render each snapshot, inspect composition.\n\nNeed ensure no animation tags left. That also prevents rsvg rendering weird. Let's do."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_dzmhm8GBqrPppOlKQ3nO6676","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\nsrc=open('pelican.svg').read()\n\n# collect leg values\nfar_anim = re.search(r'<animate attributeName=\"d\"[^>]*values=\"(M 430\\.0[^\\\"]+)\"', src)\nnear_anim = re.search(r'<animate attributeName=\"d\"[^>]*values=\"(M 445\\.0[^\\\"]+)\"', src)\nfar_vals = far_anim.group(1).split(';')\nnear_vals = near_anim.group(1).split(';')\nprint(len(far_vals), len(near_vals))\n\ndef freeze(fraction):\n    s=src\n    # remove animations\n    s=re.sub(r'<animate(?:Transform)?\\b[^>]*?/>', '', s)\n    s=re.sub(r'<animate(?:Transform)?\\b[^>]*?>.*?</animate(?:Transform)?>', '', s, flags=re.S)\n    # freeze leg d paths\n    idx=round(fraction*24)\n    def repl_path(m):\n        d=m.group(1); attrs=m.group(2); inner=m.group(3)\n        if d.startswith('M 430.0'):\n            return f'<path d=\"{far_vals[idx]}\"{attrs}>{inner}</path>'\n        if d.startswith('M 445.0'):\n            return f'<path d=\"{near_vals[idx]}\"{attrs}>{inner}</path>'\n        return m.group(0)\n    s=re.sub(r'<path d=\"(M [0-9. ]+)\"([^>]*)>(.*?)</path>', repl_path, s, flags=re.S)\n    deg=25+360*fraction\n    s=s.replace('transform=\"rotate(25 465 470)\"', f'transform=\"rotate({deg:.1f} 465 470)\"')\n    s=s.replace('transform=\"rotate(-25 511 470)\"', f'transform=\"rotate({-deg:.1f} 511 470)\"')\n    s=s.replace('transform=\"rotate(-25 419 470)\"', f'transform=\"rotate({-deg:.1f} 419 470)\"')\n    # set wheel spoke groups static gently different rotations by injecting before first spoke group? leave\n    open(f'freeze_{int(fraction*100):02d}.svg','w').write(s)\n    return idx,deg\nfor f in [0.25,0.5,0.75]:\n    print(f, freeze(f))\nPY\nfor f in 25 50 75; do rsvg-convert -w 1000 -h 700 freeze_$f.svg -o freeze_$f.png; done\nls -lh freeze_*.png","description":"Generate and render frozen animation phase snapshots"}}
