{"type":"thinking","text":"Scarf tails are mostly hidden by wing/body? The collar is the red thing, tails behind body? The paths may be under the body/wing due to drawing order: scarf tails are after body but before scarf collar, all before head and wing. Wing is drawn after, large shape covering the tails. Indeed wing covers area from x456-704 y220-315. So tails at x469-550,y218-260 are behind wing, only knot peeks above. We should move scarf tails to trail above/behind the neck and body, visible above wing, e.g. from knot at (548,225) toward left at y180-215 (above body top? body top around y200 at x460). Since body body top at x470 ~190, above body at y170 maybe visible against sky. For a scarf tied around neck, tails could trail behind over the back, above body. Let's design scarf at neck base around (552,214) with tails going left/up:\n- One tail path from knot (545,220) to (475,180), ending in two pointed strips at (450,175), (465,190). It would overlay body/back, visible. It will flutter.\n- Another tail lower from (548,228) to (490,205), but wing may cover. Good.\nMaybe the knot at (550,220) sits on neck. Draw tails after body and before wing, but they need be above wing to be visible. We can draw scarf group after wing, but then would overlay wing at base, which is okay if tail is above. Or draw scarf tails before wing but place them high enough above wing. Wing top edge starts at (456,220) and rises to (690,299); at x500, wing top y~216? So tails at y180-210 are above. Better.\n- Color red against white body and sky. Nice.\n\nLet's redesign scarf:\n```\n<g> animated rotate around 550,222\n  <path d=\"M548 218 C526 201 500 190 470 187 C484 198 496 209 502 219 C519 216 534 219 548 226 Z\" fill red .../>\n  <path d=\"M549 225 C528 214 507 211 487 215 C501 222 514 229 522 237 C532 233 540 232 549 234 Z\" fill darker/>\n</g>\n```\nHmm tail base at knot, ends at x470. This lays across the white back and slightly upward. Could look like a scarf. Perhaps two pointed ribbons trailing backwards with wavy shape:\nTail 1:\nM 548 220 C 522 206 496 197 465 199 C 480 209 488 217 492 226 C 510 221 531 226 546 232 Z\nTail 2:\nM 546 229 C 521 220 498 218 474 224 C 490 230 502 238 509 247 C 520 239 534 235 548 238 Z\nThese end at x465, y199/224. Wing at x465,y220ish, might cover lower; draw scarf after wing or before? Current wing covers. Move draw order after wing? If scarf drawn after wing, tails overlay wing top, okay. But knot should be in front of neck. Could draw scarf group after wing. That might make ribbon visible on top of wing/body, plausible. But at base, scarf collar already behind head.\n\nMaybe set group rotation around knot. Add animation. Draw after wing in upper group. That will overlay the wing at x500,y200? Wing top at x500 maybe 214; scarf at y202, so mostly above.\n\nLet's calculate body top around x490 ~190. So scarf tail lies over white body and maybe partially sky. Fine.\n\nCould add a trailing end like two tails red, with light cream stripes to show movement. Let's do that for more visual interest.\n\nAnother improvement: Saddle should be more visible. We can lighten the saddle and add a small nose ahead of the leg at x410. The body covers x335-532 down to y344, so saddle at y337 is fully within body unless body bottom is 344. It's hidden. Actually the saddle visible at left because body doesn't cover x322-370 at y333? Tail? Body path at x350 has bottom around y330? The saddle shows. Fine.\n\nMaybe add a bicycle bell on handlebar. No need.\n\nPotential issue: The near wing holding handlebar looks like a giant pointed flipper with a white blob gripping. Is there a more wing-like shape? It currently has a long top edge and gray primary feathers. Reads okay. Could add secondary feather layers at the tip around the grip: three small feather \"fingers\" curling around. Let's refine grip hand: Instead of blob, draw 3 feather finger shapes:\n- Three small rounded elongated shapes at (686,294), (692,300), (686,307) stretched to bar. But bar is behind. Could be nice. Current blob white oval maybe reads as a hand. Keep maybe but add line separations.\n\nHead: The eye is small and cartoonish. Good.\n\nBeak: The lower pouch is narrow and thick; maybe expand pouch downward more, but currently it looks like a second upper beak or open mouth. A pelican pouch should sag under. Here the pouch is beneath upper with a thin gap in between? Let's inspect crop: the upper beak is thick orange band, the pouch below is a large orange band with an inner gradient, joined at tip. The mouth line divides. It reads like a pelican bill. Fine. Maybe the pouch should be less like an open loop: currently there is sky/white visible between upper and lower? Crop shows a narrow beige stripe between upper and lower at the base, and they join at tip. The mouth line is dark at base. It could be interpreted as an open beak. To make closed beak, add fill between upper and lower near base, or adjust pouch path to touch upper at base. Currently pouch path starts at (655,190), upper lower edge line at (668,196), so they overlap? The mouth line at (657,195). Looking at crop, the orange upper and lower are separated by a cream highlight? The lower begins at 190 and upper bottom at 196, so overlap. The dark mouth line separates. The light stripe is the upper highlight maybe. It's okay.\n\nCould make the beak more natural by rounding tip and adding a hook. It has a dark tip. Fine.\n\nBody outline stroke color subtle. Good.\n\nOne visual issue: The front wheel's valve/reflector at top-right has a yellow shape; rear at upper left. Good.\n\nLet's animate wheel spokes by rotation. Good.\n\nNeed maybe add a small crank axle cap etc. Already.\n\nThe near leg looks like it passes over the chainring and then the chainring is behind. Fine.\n\nI think we can improve foot shape orientation: At 50% phase, the near foot is left of chainring and the leg ends at it. It looks like an orange shoe; okay.\n\nBut the leg's knee bends forward and the lower leg goes down vertically. This is a bit stiff. Could use smoothing curves. We can generate new leg paths with cubic curves and animate d. Maybe worthwhile for quality. The current angular two-segment looks like a stick figure leg; still okay for stylized vector. But pelican \"actively riding\" should have shapely legs. We can improve with a thicker thigh and thin shin? The current one has same thickness. Could use two separate paths for thigh and shin with animated endpoints, but both would need d animation. We could draw a filled leg shape? More involved. Maybe smooth via Q curves.\n\nLet's see if we can generate path with a quadratic curve for each segment:\n`M H Q c1 K Q c2 F` where c1 is control for thigh. But the path passes through K? Q from H to F? We need two Q commands: `M H Q c1 K Q c2 F` does pass through K at the end of first Q. The tangent at K first is K-c1; second starts tangent c2-K. Choose c2 such that c2-K is roughly parallel to K-c1 to smooth. For the thigh H→K, choose c1 = H + 0.5*(K-H) + perp*bulge. For shin K→F, choose c2 = K + 0.5*(F-K) + perp*bulge2, where perp sign chosen to make curve outward. The tangent mismatch could create slight kink but joint round. The current path with L has exact corner; Q would round the segment but still kink at K. Hmm.\n\nCubic `M H C c1a c1b K C c2a c2b F` with c1b = K - t1, c2a = K + t2, tangents aligned if t1 and t2 same direction. Let tangent direction at K be along vector from hip to foot? For a leg, the knee bend creates a natural angle, so a sharp-ish knee is fine. The joint is actually what makes it look like a knee. We can add a small knee circle at K with animated cx/cy. The round linejoin already gives a 11px radius curve. The crop shows angular but rounded enough. Fine.\n\nCould add feather cuff at hip; present but appears as white oval above leg. Good.\n\nLet's focus on ensuring correct visual animation. Perhaps we can install chromium from apt? Check apt list maybe."}
