{"type":"thinking","text":"No browser. Could use `resvg` via npm? It can render animations? Resvg does not support SMIL.\n\nMaybe use `sharp`? no. Not needed.\n\nLet's make improvements:\n1. Scarf tails visible and animated, drawn over wing.\n2. Move near/far foot to look more like webbed foot with toes. Maybe enlarge feet a little. Current foot at full image is a tiny orange blob; the pedal is dark. Pelican webbed feet should be obvious. Make foot 1.15x and add three toes. Add webbing lines. At full size, should read. Use orange foot with toe lines. The foot extends right; in both phases orientation level. Good.\n3. Maybe add knee joint highlights? no.\n4. Make near leg slightly thicker at thigh? We can create a separate thigh overlay shape, but path animation makes complex. Could increase stroke to 13 and dark 18. Pelican leg in nature is short/thick; current 11. Increase to 12.5.\n5. Add a small golden bell or fish? no.\n6. Maybe make body slightly less circular and more pelican-shaped with a distinct chest. It's fine.\n\n7. Ensure \"pelican sits on saddle\": maybe add a little saddle top under the body, visible on both sides. Could draw a brown saddle nose after body? If we draw the saddle after body, it would look like saddle is in front of pelican (wrong). Better add a subtle contact shadow on the saddle and a visible leather edge at body underside. We can draw a thin brown crescent under body at (335-420,338) after body, representing the saddle front edge, then leg. But body bottom covers. Hmm.\n\nMaybe shift body up 6px and saddle forward 5px, so more saddle visible, especially under tail. The body bottom would be 338, saddle top 337. That seems. Currently body bottom ~344 and saddle top 337, overlap. Saddle still visible left. Fine.\n\n8. The background sea line behind bike intersects the wheels and frame. Looks nice.\n\n9. The speed lines: in static first frame, opacity 0 at begin; screenshots don't show because rsvg ignores animation. In actual browser, visible intermittently. Good.\n10. Dust puffs at static rsvg show as small dots near rear wheel; okay.\n\nCould add directional motion to the \"sea\" and clouds? not needed.\n\nLet's look at the silhouette: The pelican's wing extends horizontally forward and its beak also extends; tail and body. It reads as a pelican. Good.\n\nMaybe the helmet color red + scarf also red, but scarf is not visible. If we make scarf more visible red, there's a cohesive accents. Good.\n\nLet's implement scarf changes and foot enhancements. Also maybe change `stroke-width` leg. Need use edit targeted.\n\nScarf current block:\n```\n    <!-- scarf tails -->\n    <g>\n      <animateTransform ... >\n      <path d=\"M547 226 C521 218 ...\"/>\n      <path d=\"M544 235 ...\"/>\n      <path .../>\n    </g>\n\n    <!-- scarf collar -->\n    ...\n```\nThen head, wing. We can move scarf group to after wing to be on top? If scarf is part of body group but after wing? We can cut. Better leave location but increase visibility by moving tails above wing. Yet wing drawn after will overlay them if lower. We can create long tails that extend up and behind body, visible above wing. But the wing top edge around x500 y216; scarf at y190-210 may be above. Let's design:\n```\n<g>\n animate rotate around 548 222\n <path d=\"M546 220 C522 203 496 192 462 193 C475 203 485 212 490 222 C509 218 531 223 547 231 Z\" fill red/>\n <path d=\"M548 229 C524 217 499 213 474 217 C489 224 501 233 507 243 C520 235 534 233 549 237 Z\" fill dark red/>\n</g>\n```\nAt x490,y? tail1 upper edge passes around y199, body top at x490 maybe y190, so it's on body. Wing top at x490 maybe y214, so tail1 is above wing; tail2 y~220-240 may be covered by wing. If drawn before wing, lower tail hidden. We want both visible. Move scarf group after wing (and after head? no, before head is okay). Since head drawn after wing, but scarf near neck could be under head. Fine.\nCould move entire scarf block to after wing path just before near leg. Then it will overlay wing and body. At the knot/collar, it might overlay neck. Nice. The animation around 548,225 rotates tail over wing. The red ribbons in front of the wing could seem like the scarf is on top, as if wind blows it over the shoulder. Plausible.\n\nBut if drawn after wing, the scarf tail overlay might cross the wing grip? only x462-550, y190-240, not near grip. Good.\nCollar drawn after wing? It would sit on neck base at x536-568, y210-236, wing at x? wing upper edge at x550 maybe 230, lower. Collar should be visible; current collar visible above wing partly. Fine.\nLet's move scarf tails + collar after wing. But in the XML, head group comes before wing. Could simply leave all in place and add a duplicate scarf overlay after wing? Not good. Move by editing: remove block, reinsert after `<!-- near wing ... -->` group closing. Need careful.\n\nAlternatively modify the source to add a new group after wing and delete old. Use a script for range replacement? Could use edit with old string and new string. The scarf block is ~15 lines. We can edit to change tail paths and then rely on being before wing view. But to put on top, we'd need move. Maybe easiest: Keep tails where they are but reshape so they extend above wing, and add a second longer scarf tail after wing (just the tail) that reads. Duplicate scarf knot? Hmm.\n\nLet's first create a high-quality scarf visible above the back:\nCurrent scarf tails at y218-260 are under wing; only knot visible. If we draw tails from knot toward upper-left, they will be above wing (wing's upper boundary at x500 maybe 216 and x470 maybe 224). At y190-215, visible. One tail can extend to x450,y180. That's enough red visible. Let's adjust current paths upward:\nTail 1:\n`M 547 219 C 522 199 494 185 463 184 C 477 196 487 207 493 217 C 511 213 532 218 546 229 Z`\nAt x463-547, y184-229. The upper part is above body contour? Body top at x463 is around 190. So it overlays body. Wing not drawn yet, but tail visible because it's above wing's top edge mostly. At x520, y~201; wing top at x520 maybe 221, so visible. At x540, y218; wing top at x540 ~233, visible. Good.\nTail 2:\n`M 548 227 C 524 212 499 207 475 210 C 490 218 502 227 508 237 C 521 230 535 229 549 234 Z`\nAt x475 y210, wing top at x475 ~224, visible; lower portions maybe slightly covered by wing. It's okay.\nAdd a third tail maybe. The scarf should have 2 tails. Good.\nDraw collar as before.\n\nThen because wing drawn after, tails upper remain visible. The lower edges may be covered, giving layered effect. Fine.\n\nMake scarf stripe highlight.\n\nFoot: update both foot paths to larger and with toes. But the foot groups are nested and transformed. Coordinates are local around pedal (511,470). Current:\n```\n<path d=\"M 503 461 C 496 467 498 475 506 476 L 532 478 C 544 479 547 472 538 468 L 514 460 Z\".../>\n```\nThis is foot from ankle (506,461) to toes (544,472). Good. We can enlarge:\n`M 501 459 C 493 465 495 476 505 478 L 535 480 C 550 481 553 471 541 466 L 515 458 Z`\nToe lines:\n`M 507 467 L 520 477 L 536 478`\n`M 512 463 L 526 474`\nMaybe 3 toes. Add web shading.\nAlso the ankle is at 511,470 center; leg ends at 511,? after parent rotation. Fine.\nFar foot similarly around 419:\n`M 409 459 C 401 465 403 476 413 478 L 443 480 C 458 481 461 471 449 466 L 423 458 Z`\nNeed the foot appears in front? It's fine.\n- Add small claw tip dark? Pelican feet don't have claws. no.\n- Pedal platform perhaps width 38; extend to 42.\n- Add foot highlight.\n\nNear leg stroke increase from 16/11 to 17/12. Far 16/11. Good maybe.\n- Add a small joint circle at knee? Since knee moves, we could animate. Not necessary.\n\nHelmet perhaps add a tiny white stripe across. There's already highlight. Fine.\n\nCould make the wing tip gripping more obvious by adding 3 finger feathers:\nCurrent hand path is one blob. Add after hand path:\n```\n<path d=\"M681 295 C687 294 692 296 695 300\"...\n<path d=\"M682 300 C688 300 692 303 693 307\"...\n```\nAlready one